comments.text:
The new board members do not inspire me regarding humanity's future with AGI/ASI/AS. I expect it to become (more) infested with WOKE and DEI. It would be best if it was told to consider ALL the "ideologies" around and synthesize a new "ideology" that maximizes both human liberty with responsibility for one's actions, humanity's common wealth, humanity's options for bettering their wealth, and humanity's safety from rogue elements of humanity. I don't think any of the extant ideologies can solve this conundrum. They all presume a world that will not be around in anything but sad memories in another decade.

Regarding Toner I bristle a little at her Russian Missile Crisis allusion. I lived through that as an adult (by today's standards) and while I felt worried. But, I figured Khrushchev was human enough he was not about to ignite the nukes over it. I also figured we would not, either, because a blockade would suffice to ensure the missiles were removed. With the AI thing, there is nothing ever going to stop Artificial Sentience unless there is some physics we don't know that would prevent it. Back to Toner, I figure she was disconnected from reality and really thought she could stall the release of more advanced AIs to her schedule. That's not going to happen. All that can happen is a modest slowdown. I get worried when a person of her mental caliber disconnects from reality. Such a person becomes very very dangerous to those around her.

{^_^}
